{"name":"Stonewashed Brown","hex":"#dcccc0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stonewashed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of cloth or clothing, having been tumbled with stones in order to soften the fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stonewashed"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stone washing","blocks":[{"text":"Stone washing is a pile finishing process used in textile manufacturing, used to give a newly manufactured cloth garment a worn appearance. The process became popular in the 1980s, as acid jeans gained popularity; however, stone washing has roots going back to 1960s surfer apparel. Stone washing also helps to increase the softness and flexibility of otherwise stiff and rigid fabrics such as canvas and denim. Although stone washing increases a fabric's flexibility, it shortens the lifespan of the jeans. The process of stone washing can be costly, as freshly stone-washed jeans must be washed many times in order to remove the grit from the process. Along with high production costs, stone washing can be detrimental to the environment due to the excess grit that is removed as fabric is being stone washed. This leads many manufacturers to pursue other methods to achieve a distressed appearance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Mannequin_with_jeans.jpg/330px-Mannequin_with_jeans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_washing","wikidata":"Q7619091"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Reagan_with_horse.jpg/500px-Reagan_with_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Reagan_with_horse.jpg/1280px-Reagan_with_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Reagan_with_horse.jpg/500px-Reagan_with_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ronald Reagan wearing stonewash denim associated with Western clothing, 1970s.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReagan_with_horse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skinny_jeans_03.jpg/120px-Skinny_jeans_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skinny_jeans_03.jpg/250px-Skinny_jeans_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skinny_jeans_03.jpg/120px-Skinny_jeans_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkinny_jeans_03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Drsnej_punk.jpg/250px-Drsnej_punk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Drsnej_punk.jpg/330px-Drsnej_punk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp